meta {
  name: List sessions
  type: http
  seq: 20
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/sessions
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200 [{ "id": 1, "name": "...", "date": "2026-10-14", "mode": "practice", "status": "live", "courseVersion": 1, "boats": [{ "deviceId": "..." }] }]

  LIST ROWS ONLY — this endpoint deliberately returns NO course geometry
  (no marks / startLine / finishLine / courseSnapshot). The Sessions pane
  renders only name, date, boats.length, courseVersion, mode and status,
  so shipping geometry meant parsing a large payload nobody read.

  Geometry lives in GET /sessions/:id, which the pane fetches when you
  select a session. There is no separate /geometry route.

  Filters (all optional, combinable):
    ?date=YYYY-MM-DD     exact day
    ?from=&to=            inclusive date range
    ?status=a,b           any of: scheduled, live, finished, abandoned

  status is filtered AFTER deriveStatus, because status is inferred on
  read (abandoned sticks; otherwise from startTime + uploaded runs), so
  it cannot be a SQL predicate.

  400 on a malformed date, from > to, or an unknown status.
}